envctl — manage keys in env files

Usage:
  envctl <cmd> [file] [args...]
  envctl [file] <KEY>            get
  envctl [file] <KEY> <VALUE>    set

Commands:
  set          [file] <KEY> [VALUE]  set or replace KEY, uncommenting if commented
  get          [file] <KEY>          print the active value; exit 1 if unset
  disable      [file] <KEY>          comment KEY out, keeping its value
  enable       [file] <KEY>          uncomment KEY
  delete       [file] <KEY>          remove KEY entirely, active and commented
  list         [file]                print active keys
  redact       [file]                filter stdin to stdout, masking secrets
  env                                print the process environment, always redacted
  completions  <shell>               print a completion script for a shell
  module       <shell>               print a cmdlet wrapper module for pwsh

Aliases: rm = delete, ls = list
File: optional when ./.env exists as a regular file

Flags:
  --dry-run   print a unified diff and write nothing
  --values    also print values
  --all       also print disabled keys
  --sort      print entries sorted by key
  --env       use the process environment instead of a file
  --no-env    skip the env file's literal values, use heuristics only
  --redact    mask secret-looking values
  --raw       never mask, and never escape control bytes
  --paranoid  apply the entropy bar to every value
  -h          print short usage
  --help      print this help
  --version   print the version this binary was built from (also -v, -V)

Redaction rules, filter mode, and guarantees: man envctl
